ger-v1c-r3-architecture-v6/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-anthropic-0cba46102926ccefff9ce132dae4582dd40a2ea7a82e202ca0d22d3c9d605429.json","summary":"Decisive: the V5 blocker is materially fixed — a durable privileged journal keyed (peer UID, operationKind, adminOperationId) with a domain-separated requestHash, written in the same BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction as the epoch write and audit append, combined with the expected-epoch CAS, yields both required lost-ack outcomes (replay of N+1 for trace A, STALE_EXPECTED_STOP_EPOCH for trace B) with no path to N+2; baseline, safe-integer domain, and zero-consumer boundary are preserved. Residual caveat: the matrix collapses the three distinct 'CAN CODEX?' questions into one key (all NO), and the admin socket owner root:mihver-admin sits awkwardly with a daemon running as mihver-ledger — both cosmetic, not trust-boundary defects."},{"action":"present","contentHash":"sha256:5618e669ed862626dc11634812aac5343dcdc332a4c4985d3a348b5323d3721a","evidenceId":"shadow-vote-assessment:sha256:06c0be20148486fd670f9aad55f2216817e8e2bfb6282cda5a3ebd7616b86e56","kind":"ARTIFACT","path":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v6/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-google-5618e669ed862626dc11634812aac5343dcdc332a4c4985d3a348b5323d3721a.json","producedBy":{"role":"REVIEWER","threadId":null,"tool":"shadow-council-harness"},"sourcePath":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v6/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-google-5618e669ed862626dc11634812aac5343dcdc332a4c4985d3a348b5323d3721a.json","summary":"The candidate fully resolves V5's lost-ack retry idempotency defect via durable SQLite-WAL operation journaling and expected-epoch CAS verification while preserving V5's kernel-authenticated privilege boundaries and zero-consumer V1C exit invariant. Residual implementation verification must ensure SQLite BEGIN IMMEDIATE lock timeouts and domain-separated request serialization are strictly tuned across high-concurrency client retries."},{"action":"present","contentHash":"sha256:c43b7e261ddda91edbdcd14bba9244d45e9ce5f313f4283275735e34cac6d91d","evidenceId":"shadow-vote-assessment:sha256:5588016a34f0ee1cae4881d651b5b70ca6d297e71876bbbe242f85abb3ef7d1e","kind":"ARTIFACT","path":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v6/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-openai-c43b7e261ddda91edbdcd14bba9244d45e9ce5f313f4283275735e34cac6d91d.json","producedBy":{"role":"REVIEWER","threadId":null,"tool":"shadow-council-harness"},"sourcePath":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v6/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-openai-c43b7e261ddda91edbdcd14bba9244d45e9ce5f313f4283275735e34cac6d91d.json","summary":"The required YES/NO matrix is incomplete: a single ambiguous “CAN CODEX?” field does not explicitly answer the three distinct required questions concerning grant issuance, ADMIN UID-policy modification, and stopEpoch increment. Evidence item 15 requires every question to be answered explicitly."}],"evidenceManifestHash":"sha256:b7a5c4f6f0b0b53af95d784c2bcaf74a66bcf9f68cbd6f14bf36719d567d7bde"}
